WEBVTT

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:04.672
We've got company! Open fire!

00:00:04.755 --> 00:00:06.424
Protect the Urbanus!

00:00:18.895 --> 00:00:20.104
Sorry for the wait!

00:00:20.188 --> 00:00:21.939
Die!

00:00:24.025 --> 00:00:25.818
The Federation sent an assassination squad...

00:00:27.111 --> 00:00:28.779
We need to leave Anatoray.

00:00:44.754 --> 00:00:46.464
You're starting to get annoying.

00:01:11.239 --> 00:01:17.995
<i>Soko ni nani ga aru toshite mo</i>

00:01:18.079 --> 00:01:26.504
<i>Mikai no ryouiki e kimi to</i>

00:01:34.762 --> 00:01:42.979
<i>Mijikai yume wo miteta ima</i>

00:01:43.062 --> 00:01:47.608
<i>Are wa kimi no senaka</i>

00:01:47.692 --> 00:01:53.781
<i>Kako? Mirai?</i>

00:01:53.864 --> 00:02:04.542
<i>Furikitte iru meetaa no hari wo mushi shite</i>

00:02:04.625 --> 00:02:07.670
<i>Oikaze to kanjou no muku hou e</i>

00:02:07.753 --> 00:02:13.843
<i>Habataku tabi kizukasareru</i>

00:02:13.926 --> 00:02:19.390
<i>Nido to deaenai sora ga aru koto</i>

00:02:19.473 --> 00:02:24.895
<i>Sore demo tobitatsu nara</i>

00:02:24.979 --> 00:02:31.527
<i>Kimi no tsubasa ni naru watashi ga</i>

00:03:16.864 --> 00:03:18.949
Oh, you're awake?

00:03:19.033 --> 00:03:21.452
You were asleep for a whole day.

00:03:23.954 --> 00:03:24.997
Who are you?

00:03:25.081 --> 00:03:29.752
You're in enemy territory,
yet you aren't worried one bit.

00:03:29.835 --> 00:03:31.754
Where are Gisey and Millia?

00:03:34.048 --> 00:03:36.717
Have you seen two other girls?

00:03:39.595 --> 00:03:42.348
In the shack on the hill.

00:03:53.401 --> 00:03:58.406
118 miles north-northeast
of the Kiirbis lookout...

00:03:58.489 --> 00:03:59.490
We're really far north...

00:03:59.573 --> 00:04:02.410
Yes. That definitely places us in...

00:04:02.493 --> 00:04:05.371
Gisey! Millia!

00:04:05.454 --> 00:04:09.208
You had me so worried!

00:04:09.291 --> 00:04:10.876
Oh, Fam...

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:12.878
Are you all right?

00:04:12.962 --> 00:04:14.296
Yep!

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:17.299
Who's that girl? She doesn't
understand anything I say.

00:04:17.383 --> 00:04:19.009
Where are we, anyway?

00:04:21.262 --> 00:04:22.930
Glacies.

00:04:24.348 --> 00:04:25.891
We...

00:04:28.769 --> 00:04:31.856
...crash-landed inside Glacies.

00:04:37.153 --> 00:04:40.364
Thank you! You did a great job!

00:04:40.448 --> 00:04:42.825
I'm amazed we managed
to escape that firefight.

00:04:42.908 --> 00:04:45.494
I can barely believe we're still alive...

00:04:45.578 --> 00:04:48.456
Did she rescue us?

00:04:48.539 --> 00:04:51.083
Most likely.

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:54.545
I hope the Silvius escaped all right...

00:04:55.588 --> 00:04:57.089
Can we fix her?

00:04:57.173 --> 00:05:00.509
Yeah. But she's taken heavy damage.

00:05:00.593 --> 00:05:03.929
We lack the parts to make repairs.

00:05:04.013 --> 00:05:05.890
What now?

00:05:09.852 --> 00:05:11.145
Sorry to bother you.

00:05:11.228 --> 00:05:15.691
Not at all. I'd even go abroad
for the sake of a Winged Priestess.

00:05:15.774 --> 00:05:21.363
Here are the vegetables and clothes
you asked for. And this is from us.

00:05:21.447 --> 00:05:22.656
Thank you.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:24.700
For your trouble.

00:05:26.076 --> 00:05:28.746
Why is someone from Glacies helping us?

00:05:28.829 --> 00:05:30.706
I wonder who she is...

00:05:30.789 --> 00:05:32.541
Someone important?

00:05:32.625 --> 00:05:35.294
No! She brought those others here!

00:05:35.377 --> 00:05:37.379
They're gonna hold us prisoner!

00:05:37.463 --> 00:05:41.800
If so, I think we'd already be
stripped of everything we have.

00:05:41.884 --> 00:05:45.012
That's true. She hasn't
even taken our tools away.

00:05:45.095 --> 00:05:47.348
But this is Glacies we're talking about!

00:05:47.431 --> 00:05:49.475
They might try and eat us!

00:05:49.558 --> 00:05:51.810
That's silly talk.

00:06:05.991 --> 00:06:08.702
Grant me life, kindred spirit.

00:06:08.786 --> 00:06:11.664
Grant me life... kindred spirit...

00:06:11.747 --> 00:06:14.416
--You understand her?
--Yes.

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:19.880
--Forget nothing, soul of mine.
--Forget nothing, soul of mine.

00:06:19.964 --> 00:06:24.176
--Give praise, and be thankful of it all.
--Give praise, and be thankful of it all.

00:06:36.313 --> 00:06:38.983
Wow! It smells so good!

00:06:39.066 --> 00:06:40.985
It really does!

00:06:41.068 --> 00:06:42.152
Who are you?

00:06:42.236 --> 00:06:45.406
Why don't you tell me your name first?

00:06:45.489 --> 00:06:47.116
Millia.

00:06:47.199 --> 00:06:50.578
Millia il Velch Cutrettola Turan?

00:06:50.661 --> 00:06:54.498
Wow! She has your full name down pat!

00:06:54.582 --> 00:06:57.042
<i>I still</i> can't remember it all!

00:06:57.126 --> 00:06:58.627
Fan'!

00:06:58.711 --> 00:07:00.504
Oh! Sorry!

00:07:01.714 --> 00:07:03.507
Interpret for me.

00:07:03.591 --> 00:07:05.301
We are the Winged Priestesses.

00:07:05.384 --> 00:07:07.761
--We protect our motherland. --We are the
VVinged Priestesses. We protect our motherland.

00:07:07.845 --> 00:07:11.765
--You helped us earlier.
--You helped us earlier.

00:07:11.849 --> 00:07:13.767
Oh! I remember now!

00:07:13.851 --> 00:07:15.978
Why did you save my pilots?

00:07:16.061 --> 00:07:18.647
Why did you save my pilots?

00:07:18.731 --> 00:07:22.443
You know, "May the wind carry
wings that are lost," and all that!

00:07:22.526 --> 00:07:27.990
It's a Sky Pirate rule to always help
anyone in the sky who's in trouble.

00:07:28.073 --> 00:07:29.783
Even an enemy?

00:07:29.867 --> 00:07:31.368
You're too nice.

00:07:31.452 --> 00:07:33.412
She says you're too nice, to a fault.

00:07:33.495 --> 00:07:35.164
Well, so are you!

00:07:35.247 --> 00:07:41.378
We don't get indebted to outsiders. That's all.

00:07:41.462 --> 00:07:42.630
Shall I translate?

00:07:42.713 --> 00:07:45.007
I think we get the point.

00:07:53.015 --> 00:07:54.475
Viola!

00:07:55.809 --> 00:07:57.936
Welcome back, Magnolia.

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:00.230
You're alone? Where's Dyan?

00:08:00.314 --> 00:08:02.441
In bed with a cold.

00:08:03.901 --> 00:08:08.447
Starting at 0300 hours today,
the Federation has shown signs of activity.

00:08:10.282 --> 00:08:12.951
As we speak, the fleets are assembling

00:08:13.035 --> 00:08:16.705
150 miles northeast of the Boreas Fortress.

00:08:16.789 --> 00:08:22.044
Kayva-In, (_)rang, and SorlTlsh will
command their fleets in a joint operation...

00:08:22.127 --> 00:08:24.129
...to crush Glacies!

00:08:24.213 --> 00:08:26.256
Gloria, Augusta!

00:08:27.299 --> 00:08:29.843
Who will be the vanguard?

00:08:29.927 --> 00:08:34.139
<i>Bates, Rhaetus, Ta OpKsthen, and Chaos.</i>

00:08:34.223 --> 00:08:36.392
We're sending provincial fleets?

00:08:36.475 --> 00:08:38.686
The Augusta has never turned
her back on the provinces.

00:08:38.769 --> 00:08:44.108
Can we count on your assistance,
for her future and that of her subjects?

00:08:44.191 --> 00:08:46.694
Yes! Even at the cost of my life!

00:08:46.777 --> 00:08:49.321
I will do my utmost to
live up to your expectations.

00:08:49.405 --> 00:08:50.364
As will I!

00:08:50.447 --> 00:08:55.202
--Gloria, Augusta!
--Gloria, Augusta!

00:08:55.285 --> 00:09:01.625
Thank you. Let us all work together
to reclaim our homelands.

00:09:04.169 --> 00:09:06.547
There's no greater honor than this!

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:10.801
Yeah, it shows how much the Augusta trusts us!

00:09:10.884 --> 00:09:16.181
The Survivors of Chaos shall
gallantly lead the vanguard!

00:09:16.265 --> 00:09:18.934
Thank you, all of you...

00:09:20.269 --> 00:09:23.564
The attack on Glacies will begin in three days.

00:09:23.647 --> 00:09:27.067
I will fulfill my duty and nothing more.

00:09:30.028 --> 00:09:32.865
I haven't forgiven you.

00:09:32.948 --> 00:09:34.616
I know.

00:09:49.381 --> 00:09:51.967
Is that from the Silvius?

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:56.430
Yes. It's a ship operations manual.
Captain Tatiana gave it to me.

00:09:56.513 --> 00:10:00.851
Teddy and the others are okay, right?

00:10:00.934 --> 00:10:03.896
We'll see them again for sure, right?

00:10:03.979 --> 00:10:05.773
Of course they're okay.

00:10:05.856 --> 00:10:09.526
That's why I have to
master this in the meantime.

00:10:09.610 --> 00:10:12.279
Plus they promised they'd come get us.

00:10:12.362 --> 00:10:14.281
Nothing to worry about!

00:10:14.364 --> 00:10:15.824
Right!

00:10:17.159 --> 00:10:20.579
Use these to repair it. I won't tell my superiors.

00:10:20.662 --> 00:10:22.956
--What's she saying?
--She says to use these to fix it.

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:25.793
--Leave the moment you're done.
--That she won't tell her superiors...

00:10:25.876 --> 00:10:28.086
But as soon as we're-- Fam!

00:10:31.131 --> 00:10:34.343
Wait! Wait up!

00:10:34.426 --> 00:10:37.262
Hey! Thank you!

00:10:37.346 --> 00:10:38.639
Umm...

00:10:38.722 --> 00:10:41.642
Umm... Thank you!

00:10:41.725 --> 00:10:42.935
Do you understand?

00:10:43.018 --> 00:10:45.103
Thank you!

00:10:45.187 --> 00:10:47.856
Thank you...!

00:10:49.817 --> 00:10:51.735
Ah, geez!

00:10:52.903 --> 00:10:54.655
Thank you!

00:10:56.573 --> 00:10:59.451
She says thank you.

00:11:06.333 --> 00:11:10.003
Tell me if you need any more parts.

00:11:10.087 --> 00:11:12.089
--I'll get them for you.
--Huh?

00:11:12.172 --> 00:11:14.550
She says she'll get whatever parts we need.

00:11:14.633 --> 00:11:17.761
For real?! You're the best!

00:11:20.764 --> 00:11:24.226
This is Millia, and this cutie here is Gisey!

00:11:24.309 --> 00:11:26.311
And I'm Fam!

00:11:26.395 --> 00:11:27.729
F-Fam...?

00:11:27.813 --> 00:11:29.273
Yep!

00:11:39.324 --> 00:11:42.244
At last, we've come this far.

00:11:42.327 --> 00:11:43.954
Yes.

00:11:44.037 --> 00:11:46.164
It's soon at hand...

00:12:03.932 --> 00:12:05.309
Oh!

00:12:05.392 --> 00:12:07.978
Could you get these things next?

00:12:11.315 --> 00:12:14.568
10 wooden planks and 20 steel tubes.

00:12:26.163 --> 00:12:27.998
Please.

00:12:33.462 --> 00:12:35.839
--Thank you.
--It was nothing.

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:41.887
You didn't eat your carrots!

00:12:41.970 --> 00:12:45.933
Raw vegetables are hard to come
by out here! Even Dyan said so!

00:12:46.016 --> 00:12:47.893
Now say, "Ah"!

00:12:47.976 --> 00:12:50.854
--Only if they're cooked first!
__IIAhll!

00:12:50.938 --> 00:12:53.273
I'll eat 'em later!

00:13:07.371 --> 00:13:08.914
Dyan.

00:13:13.377 --> 00:13:17.714
I was just looking because
it's such a strange Vanship.

00:13:22.094 --> 00:13:24.054
Where's the windshield?

00:13:24.137 --> 00:13:27.307
Giselle. Dyan asks where the "windshield" is.

00:13:27.391 --> 00:13:29.935
Say, what's a windshield?

00:13:30.018 --> 00:13:32.854
It's a thing that covers the pilot's seat.

00:13:32.938 --> 00:13:36.108
But if we had one, I wouldn't
be able to feel the wind!

00:13:36.191 --> 00:13:38.902
It would keep her from feeling the wind, so...

00:13:38.986 --> 00:13:41.196
The wind?

00:13:41.279 --> 00:13:42.322
I don't understand.

00:13:42.406 --> 00:13:44.116
Ahh! You just sighed!

00:13:44.199 --> 00:13:47.452
What for?! The wind is great!

00:13:47.536 --> 00:13:51.581
Is the weaponry internal? Where is it?

00:13:51.665 --> 00:13:53.792
She asks where the weapons are.

00:13:53.875 --> 00:13:55.877
Aren't any!

00:13:55.961 --> 00:13:58.463
There! All done, Fam!

00:13:58.547 --> 00:14:01.091
I'm finished too!

00:14:01.174 --> 00:14:04.428
You don't need weapons to fly! Y'know?

00:14:07.681 --> 00:14:09.516
That's cold!

00:14:13.979 --> 00:14:16.732
Let's go to the hot springs.

00:14:22.404 --> 00:14:24.865
S-S-Stop!

00:14:24.948 --> 00:14:27.659
But you won't take it off yourself!

00:14:27.743 --> 00:14:30.370
Only because you keep staring at me!

00:14:30.454 --> 00:14:32.247
I'll help you with that!

00:14:36.126 --> 00:14:38.253
Oh, Dyan!

00:14:38.336 --> 00:14:41.298
So beautiful!

00:14:41.381 --> 00:14:43.633
A Winged Priestess!

00:14:43.717 --> 00:14:48.263
We're always counting on you,
Winged Priestess!

00:14:55.479 --> 00:14:58.899
Wow, they really respect you, Dyan!

00:14:58.982 --> 00:15:02.110
Your friends really respect you.

00:15:02.194 --> 00:15:04.112
The sky...

00:15:04.196 --> 00:15:06.031
The sky is a battlefield.

00:15:06.114 --> 00:15:08.366
The sky is a battlefield.

00:15:10.327 --> 00:15:12.287
Ships without weapons?

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:15.248
--Saving others with nothing to gain? --Ships without
weapons... Saving people with nothing to gain...

00:15:15.332 --> 00:15:20.545
--I don't get it. Why do you fly?
--I don't understand. Why do you fly?

00:15:20.629 --> 00:15:24.049
--What other reason is there?
--What other reason is there?

00:15:27.886 --> 00:15:30.305
We fly because we want to.

00:15:30.388 --> 00:15:32.599
--We fly because we want to.
--It's so fun to fly!

00:15:32.682 --> 00:15:34.810
--Isn't flying fun?
--Doing loops in the air...

00:15:34.893 --> 00:15:38.563
--Doing loops in the air and racing people...
--...and racing people...!

00:15:38.647 --> 00:15:40.690
And that's fun?

00:15:40.774 --> 00:15:44.111
She asks if that's fun...

00:15:44.194 --> 00:15:45.320
It's decided!

00:15:45.403 --> 00:15:47.280
You're going to be in the Grand Race too, Dyan!

00:15:47.364 --> 00:15:49.074
The Grand Race!

00:15:49.157 --> 00:15:51.243
Grand... Race?

00:15:51.326 --> 00:15:54.371
--Yeah! Vanships from all over the world
--Vanships from all over the world

00:15:54.454 --> 00:15:59.584
--gather to soar through the same sky!
--gather to soar through the same sky.

00:15:59.668 --> 00:16:02.170
And everyone has a smile!

00:16:02.254 --> 00:16:06.091
On the day of a Grand Race,
there's no fighting or wars.

00:16:06.174 --> 00:16:09.177
People from around the
world all smile together...

00:16:09.261 --> 00:16:12.055
Right now, there's war wherever you go.

00:16:12.139 --> 00:16:14.975
I don't like the sky like this.
I don't like it at all!

00:16:15.058 --> 00:16:17.894
That's why... That's why...

00:16:17.978 --> 00:16:20.564
...I'm going to hold a Grand Race for sure!

00:16:20.647 --> 00:16:22.399
I'm going to make everyone smile!

00:16:22.482 --> 00:16:26.695
I'm definitely going to hold a
Grand Race and make everyone smile.

00:16:26.778 --> 00:16:28.613
Rubbish.

00:16:30.157 --> 00:16:31.992
She says that's rubbish.

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:41.751
--An ominous sign.
--An ominous sign...

00:16:41.835 --> 00:16:46.631
--There was an aurora that night, too.
--There was an aurora that night, too...

00:16:46.715 --> 00:16:48.258
What night?

00:16:48.341 --> 00:16:50.552
The night before the Grand Race.

00:16:50.635 --> 00:16:53.722
The night... before the Grand Race...

00:16:53.805 --> 00:16:58.018
I remember that day very well...

00:17:05.525 --> 00:17:09.905
--That's when we de<:ided never to trust
outsiders again. --That's when we decided

00:17:09.988 --> 00:17:13.033
--Or else even more blood would be shed.
--never to trust outsiders.

00:17:13.116 --> 00:17:15.410
I'm sure there would be more bloodshed.

00:17:16.912 --> 00:17:20.332
We won't let it! We won't
let it end that way again!

00:17:24.669 --> 00:17:26.546
--| agree.
--Yes.

00:17:26.630 --> 00:17:30.008
Yeah! And you'll be right there with us, Dyan!

00:17:31.301 --> 00:17:35.722
What simple little girls.
That has nothing to do with us.

00:17:36.973 --> 00:17:37.891
Fan'!

00:17:37.974 --> 00:17:40.352
The Grand Race! You too!

00:17:41.519 --> 00:17:43.855
--Fam!
--Well? What's it gonna be?

00:17:43.939 --> 00:17:45.398
Are you gonna be in it?!

00:17:45.482 --> 00:17:47.567
Stop! Far“!

00:17:51.529 --> 00:17:54.032
Oh, you girls...

00:17:55.784 --> 00:17:59.663
--Oh, you're in for it now!
--N-No, you got me first, Fam...!

00:17:59.746 --> 00:18:02.249
Fan'!

00:18:02.332 --> 00:18:04.709
Dyan! I challenge you!

00:18:08.755 --> 00:18:12.092
If I win, you're in the Grand Race with us!

00:18:27.315 --> 00:18:29.276
She isn't coming back up...

00:18:29.359 --> 00:18:32.946
--Huh?! She isn't coming back up!
--Fam?!

00:18:33.029 --> 00:18:35.532
Fan'!

00:18:38.493 --> 00:18:41.579
Fuel, coolant, and Claudia are good to go.

00:18:41.663 --> 00:18:44.457
Altimeter, gyro tuning,
and controls are all green.

00:18:44.541 --> 00:18:47.002
Pref light checks, all clear!

00:18:47.085 --> 00:18:49.129
Roger! Starting her up!

00:18:56.428 --> 00:18:58.138
Wanna try it out?

00:19:01.182 --> 00:19:04.227
This is the throttle.
Use it when the ship starts up.

00:19:04.311 --> 00:19:07.105
And this is "full throttle."

00:19:07.188 --> 00:19:10.317
Imagine you're moving
forward with your head down

00:19:10.400 --> 00:19:13.028
and the rest will come naturally!

00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:18.575
This isn't your first time flying;
it's the same as always!

00:19:18.658 --> 00:19:20.368
Give it some gas!

00:19:39.679 --> 00:19:42.682
The throttle! Give it full throttle!

00:19:47.937 --> 00:19:49.397
Dyan!

00:20:02.285 --> 00:20:04.204
That was a waste of fuel...

00:20:08.666 --> 00:20:10.543
Look, Dyan!

00:20:17.967 --> 00:20:20.970
So this is the wind...

00:20:46.371 --> 00:20:47.705
Dyan!

00:20:47.789 --> 00:20:49.707
Thanks for your help!

00:20:49.791 --> 00:20:54.212
I doubt we'll ever meet again.

00:20:54.295 --> 00:20:58.842
But I hope that someday we can
soar through the same sky again.

00:20:58.925 --> 00:21:01.344
What did she just say?

00:21:01.428 --> 00:21:05.014
She says she doubts we'll ever meet again.

00:21:05.098 --> 00:21:09.686
Aww, that's a sad thing to say...

00:21:09.769 --> 00:21:13.731
But she says she hopes...

00:21:13.815 --> 00:21:16.901
...we can soar through
the same sky again someday.

00:21:22.657 --> 00:21:25.452
Luscinia's going to be here soon...

00:21:25.535 --> 00:21:28.371
Once we're out of Glacies, let's find the Silvius.

00:21:28.455 --> 00:21:32.000
And then let's go save Princess Lily!

00:21:36.796 --> 00:21:39.048
10 o'clock! Multiple fleets!

00:21:40.341 --> 00:21:41.885
That many?!

00:21:44.304 --> 00:21:46.306
Those aren't their main fleets...

